{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558637-veddartha-embracing-using-ventru-s-blood","id":1558637,"title":"Veddartha embracing using Ventru's blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-04T09:29:21-08:00","id":1558637,"title":"Veddartha embracing using Ventru's blood","content":"I remember reading years ago that Veddartha (said to be 4th generation, has multiple 5th generation childer) embraced some of his childer using Ventru's blood, with a sort of proxy embrace. The blood of Ventru was in a cup, which was possessed by Veddartha and used a few times in history.<br /> <br /> Searching around online I can't find any evidence of this, but I remember reading it very vividly, perhaps in one of the V20 books, or on one of the forums? Does anyone have any recollection of anything similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T13:02:14-08:00","id":1558641,"title":"","content":"Again, forum ate my edit...<br /> Here we go again, I will delete the og ... eventually<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I can't recall anything like that<br /> Which not means it is not a thing, just the lack of my knowledge and memory<br /> <br /> But I think what you have here is the mix and mingle of several things, blending together<br /> <br /> Veddartha is a bit of an enigma and a mess when it comes to Vampire and Mithras not really helps the case<br /> Nor the fact the Ventrue Antediluvian despite his alleged death either by the hand of Troile in the First or a bunch of Brujah around the fall of the Second city was quite active and Embraced left and right up untill the lates child Ueruic/ Erik Eigermann (the sire of the original Hardestadt ) and his broodmate Antonius the Gaul (the later member of the Triumvirate of Constantinople) around 600 BC<br /> We have at least two Vampires from the 5th Generation who are the childe of Veddartha, Balthazar and Maltheas<br /> On the other hand? The Danava believe themselves to be the guardians of their Antediluvian whom they call Veddhartha. These Danava claim that the Ventrue are in fact an errant antitribu bloodline of the Danava<br /> So despite slain, the Antediluvian Emraced quite frequently and now slumbers somewhere in India...<br /> Mithras also claims to be the Child of Veddartha... but he is of the 4th Generation. Diabelire? Perhaps...<br /> Or more likely what we have is the classic case if the shared name the Ventrue love to use; like Hardestadt the Elder and Hardestadt the Younger<br /> Veddartha the Elder is the Antediluvian and Sire of Mithras, and Veddartha the Younger is the the 4th Generation one, sire of others<br /> <br /> To support this - or complicate - we have a nice little relic from the Road of Kings, p. 76. <b>Veddartha's Chalice</b><br /> \u200bThe Chalice of Veddartha appears in many of the parables and legends that Scions tell of the First City and the rise of Clan Ventrue. Supposedly, the Ventrue clan founder drank his Sire's blood from this cup, rather than feasting directly from his veins, during his embrace. This is an important detail \u2014 Veddartha evidently had the strength, even after being drained of his life's blood, to raise a glass and choose to drink.<br /> <br /> So the name again pops up, in relation of the Antediluvian, but this time way back to the First City, and the relic once held Enoch's blood...<br /> <br /> And here comes a funny part, and where the whole bood thing could come; relics this one and the one of their clanbook<br /> <br /> <br /> Clanbook: Venture p.14 talks about the Ventrue Antediluvian's Palace in the First City and how he turned it into a Fortress after a talk with Caine about the future and the threat of the Secret Masters and then gathered very interesting relics like the Tapestry of Blood, the head of Medusa, the claws of Fenris, the Fearie Bridge and Oromazus' Mist alegedly with the plan, as he stated to the other Antediluvians who questioned him about why he hoarded those tings &quot;When the time has come, we shall use these tools to recreate the World&quot;<br /> <br /> The Tapestry of Blood is actually detailed in Vampire Storytellers Handbook, p. 140; The tapestry is a huge and ornate wall hanging, woven in scintillating hues by obviously expert hands, and adorned with patterns that seem to change as one looks at them. To properly use the item, it must be saturated with at least 10 blood points. It will then show a variety of scenes in its weavings; tales vary as to precisely what can be viewed there, but accounts have stated things as different as the Great Flood, the near future, the founding of the Second City, the secret weaknesses of a mighty Methuselah, and Gehenna.<br /> All the visions, however, relate directly to the Kindred, past, present or future. There is so much to see in the tapestry that gazing into its depths requires a full night and a roll of Perception + Occult; the more successes gained, the more useful or relevant the information acquired. A botch may either give misleading information or lead to the discovery of a horrible truth about the Kindred, resulting in a Derangement.<br /> <br /> The head of Medusa probably intended to be the head that Perseus chopped off, but since the First City predates every other city and Perseus was the son of King Acrisius of Argos daughter, Dana\u00eb? It bit rules out that possibility.<br /> On the other hand, when the first Clanbooks came out, crossover was not something devilish and many supplement was designed in mind of a potentiall crossover games, so Medusa likely the Medusa wh was a Galliard of the first Black Fury pack, and after her death became a Totem of War ( The Black Furies say that when Medusa, the last of the Medusae finally died, Artemis (an avatar of Luna herself) coaxed Pegasus into existence from her corpse)<br /> Now the preserved head of a Garou who later ascended to become a Totem? A neat little relic<br /> <br /> The claws of Fenris actually fits into this narrartive quite well, not long ago we had a little side discussin about Odin and the Fenris in another topic and while the time line not entirely lines up, it is not that out of the realm of possibility Great Fenris lost a few claws, even a whole paw when he hunted and fought on the material plane and like with Medusa's head, that paw or set of claws ended up in the Ventrue Antediluvian's collection<br /> <br /> There is no mention of the Fearie Bridge in any supplement, so what the hell it is? Probably something Changeling related. Your guess is as good as mine<br /> <br /> Oromazus' Mist is another question mark.<br /> But Oromazus is the Greek form of Ahura-Mazda, who represents truth, light, and goodness and who is the direct antithesis to Ahriman (Angra Mainyu), the destructive spirit of chaos, darkness, and evil. What his &quot;mist&quot; could be? Very good question<br /> <br /> <br /> Clanbook: Venture p.16 talks about what happened after the Flood, how Caine talked with the Ventrue Antediluvian before went off the map. He organized the built of the Second City where he h\u00edd the mightiest artifacts he managed to rescue from the First City. Also there the Ventrue Antediluvian burried a clay pot dilled with the Vitae of Caine firmly beliving those treasures would be safe even after the Second City fell - and will be ready to be used by all the kindred when the time is right.<br /> <br /> So we have a cup that once held Enoch's blood and used to help the tachnically self-Embrace of the Ventrue Antediluvian and a pot filled with Caine's vitae - and a bunch of other artifacts<br /> <br /> I think - could be wrong - your memory mixed all those things together and came up with what you wrote\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 03-05-2026, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-04T20:37:31-08:00","id":1558647,"title":"","content":"I don't recall this from any official material. Ventrue is in a weird spot. By some accounts he's dead but apparently 4th gens were still being embraced long after he had died. He could have been faking his death, of course. There's been some hints that Set diablarized an Antediluvian (Typhon) and that Typhon could have been Ventrue. Occasionally he takes over Set's body and embraces new 4th gen vampires. The Veddartha cup seems like another plausible explanation for how new 4th gen Ventrue were being created after he had died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T13:49:02-08:00","id":1558666,"title":"","content":"Word of Justin Achilli (revised edition editor) is that Ventrue's fortitude 10 power was the ability to soak death. So he &quot;dies&quot; pops up later when he wants to and does as he desires with everyone thinking him dead.<br /> <br /> Not my favorite interpretation, but definitely makes things work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T07:08:07-08:00","id":1558678,"title":"","content":"Realistically the Mithras and Maltheas sire problem is most likely an editorial issue and mistake (using an established name and not checking its history) but one that makes a fun mystery.<br /> <br /> Here's a few of theories I'd like to posit:<br /> <br /> 1. [Ventrue] using his mastery of Dominate and Fortitude, allows/forces a direct Childe to diablerize him, but takes over the body. This is to avoid the curse of the Methuselah's Thirst.<br /> <br /> 2. [Ventrue] is both [Ventrue] and Veddartha, and perhaps many others. High level Dominate [lv9 Puppet Master] allows you to practically clone yourself by conditioning someone else to think they are you. You can see similar with Hardestat the Elder and Hardestat the Younger/Jurgen Von Verden and eventually the failed Hardestat the Youngest/Jan Pieterzoon. (This last bit was one of the plot points of the Gehenna novel.)<br /> <br /> 3. Here's a wild one. The modern Ventrue and Brujah [and their variations, Danava, Antitribu, &quot;True&quot;] are sibling bloodlines of a single Antedeluvian. So where's this one come from? Well it hinges on a line in Clan Book Revised: Ventrue. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <i><b>[CbR-V] PG12</b> &quot;Trying to hold the disparate community together, [Ventrue] attempted to listen to and resolve the Cainites' problems - even the depredations of his sister, the witch.&quot;</i> </div> </div> </div>Its a very curious line &quot;<i>even the depredations of his sister, the witch</i>&quot;. First we have the idea that [Ventrue] had a sister. Is this a blood/brood sibling? A biological sister? Secondly, [Ventrue] is defending against this sister's depredations. A depredation is another word for attack or pillage. Third this sibling is called &quot;the witch.&quot; Are they a mage? Well perhaps but it seems instead of being <i>a witch </i>they are being referred to as<i> the witch.</i> Its a title or honorific. Interestingly enough in modern times there's this little clan called the Brujah that borrows the Romantic (Spanish) word for witch as their name even though they have nothing to do with sorcery. This said clan seems to have a real big problem with the Ventrue as a whole and is constantly at odds with them.<br /> <br /> My favorite interpretation of this is that [Ventrue] was actually Ilyes and that this sister is Troile. Troile originally being what we would consider Ventrue blood until she diablerizes her brother and creates her own brood that becomes known as the Brujah. [Ventrue]'s blood continues on otherwise due to having had sired a large brood, through the Ventrue bloodline. This helps explain [Ventrue]'s disapearance, Troile's ascendance to 3rd gen, and the antipathy of the two clans even though they have forgotten their origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-10T14:09:12-07:00","id":1558774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558637-veddartha-embracing-using-ventru-s-blood?p=1558678#post1558678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite interpretation of this is that [Ventrue] was actually Ilyes and that this sister is Troile. Troile originally being what we would consider Ventrue blood until she diablerizes her brother and creates her own brood that becomes known as the Brujah. [Ventrue]'s blood continues on otherwise due to having had sired a large brood, through the Ventrue bloodline. This helps explain [Ventrue]'s disapearance, Troile's ascendance to 3rd gen, and the antipathy of the two clans even though they have forgotten their origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spinning on the word of Achil mentioned above where Fortitude 10 let's you soak final death modify it so it says 'even if the progenitor of the clan is diablerized or killed my line continues'. Ventrue is the line of all of them.<br /> <br /> It's still soaking death but in a completely ventrue way. No Cappadocian, saulot or ravnos here. Ventrue lives on through his lineage. The king is dead. Long live the clan of kings.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-10T20:06:00-07:00","id":1558782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558637-veddartha-embracing-using-ventru-s-blood#post1558637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading years ago that Veddartha (said to be 4th generation, has multiple 5th generation childer) embraced some of his childer using Ventru's blood, with a sort of proxy embrace. The blood of Ventru was in a cup, which was possessed by Veddartha and used a few times in history.<br /> <br /> Searching around online I can't find any evidence of this, but I remember reading it very vividly, perhaps in one of the V20 books, or on one of the forums? Does anyone have any recollection of anything similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Veddartha is [Ventrue]. The thing is WW back in the day chose inconsistencies.<br /> <br /> The main problem was Maltheas on Transylvania Chronicles 2 because he appeared as 5th, but the thing is that most of those NPCs had an explanation chapters before were they were explicitly described as &quot;appear to be of a higher generation&quot;, just like Hardestadt the Younger (which was 6th during the Convention of Thorns but appears as 5th).<br /> <br /> I also remember when London by Night came out that was supposed to end the discussion by the writer stating that Mithras was the Ventrue Antediluvian childer before it was published and so it was, but, you know, where's the fun in ending a discussion?<br /> <br /> That's the WHY.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-26T02:27:34-07:00","id":1559028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558637-veddartha-embracing-using-ventru-s-blood?p=1558782#post1558782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Veddartha is [Ventrue]. The thing is WW back in the day chose inconsistencies.<br /> <br /> The main problem was Maltheas on Transylvania Chronicles 2 because he appeared as 5th, but the thing is that most of those NPCs had an explanation chapters before were they were explicitly described as &quot;appear to be of a higher generation&quot;, just like Hardestadt the Younger (which was 6th during the Convention of Thorns but appears as 5th).<br /> <br /> I also remember when London by Night came out that was supposed to end the discussion by the writer stating that Mithras was the Ventrue Antediluvian childer before it was published and so it was, but, you know, where's the fun in ending a discussion?<br /> <br /> That's the WHY.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Veddartha is the name given as <b><i>the sire of Mithras</i></b>, as of 1e a World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> From the fact Mithras is given as 4th generation and a Ventrue, it had been <b><i>assumed </i></b>by the fanbase that this vampire was the Ventrue antediluvian, though <i>even back then</i> the matter of generation by embrace x <i>effective </i>generation, that might involve some unstated degree of diablerie, was quite slippery. More so in fact, might be said.<br /> <br /> <i>Everything</i> about this assertion has always hinged on the idea that Mithras' claim to be a childe of the Ventrue antediluvian is true - when Mithras <b>also</b> happens to be such a brazen high octane liar/snake oil merchant to the point of <i>playing the role of solar deity while being a vampire</i>, meaning that <b>lying about a chunk of the history of the clan to the younger generations</b> and using the name of his long absent (methuselah) sire as that of the ventrue antediluvian for added (fabricated) legitimacy IS perfectly in character for him too.<br /> <br /> (Not even going into his final death and the whole reverse diablerie-fusion shenanigans with Assamite Antitribu Monty Coven...)<br /> <br /> <br /> So, things were sketchy all along. The introduction of Maltheas on Transylvania Chronicles 2 - that admitedly, seemed to have no actual function whatsoever in the book beyond introducing this poisoned easter egg, that i can remember - simply opened a can of worms in one of the most explosive ways possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-26-2026, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-28T07:09:21-07:00","id":1559055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>twig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1558637-veddartha-embracing-using-ventru-s-blood#post1558637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading years ago that Veddartha (said to be 4th generation, has multiple 5th generation childer) embraced some of his childer using Ventru's blood, with a sort of proxy embrace. The blood of Ventru was in a cup, which was possessed by Veddartha and used a few times in history.<br /> <br /> Searching around online I can't find any evidence of this, but I remember reading it very vividly, perhaps in one of the V20 books, or on one of the forums? Does anyone have any recollection of anything similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this sounds quite close to tales of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/True_Vessel\" target=\"_blank\">True Vessel</a> in the Clan of Death's legendry, so it could be a case of incidental conflation-confusion of antediluvians (what in itself could lead to some interesting misinformation, rumors and more as myths associated with a clan migrate to and get adapted in unexpected manners to another as centuries and millenia go by).<br /> <br /> That said, there are tales of the Ventrue founder collecting a variety of supernatural treasures in the First or Second City era as either keepsakes or heirlooms for its descendants and a vessel with its own vitae might or not be included among them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-28-2026, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}